<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:35Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Myanmar: Is the US undermining the EU's diplomatic blockade?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aae640ab10896233bf70cba46eb9513bff4ed4eced9df5ecf2d655e2f8cc0ab5</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T15:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-is-the-us-undermining-the-eu-s-diplomatic-blockade/a-79778863--db2dea3e5776.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-is-the-us-undermining-the-eu-s-diplomatic-blockade/a-79778863?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With the US reopening talks with Myanmar's military-backed government, and several Southeast Asian countries restarting diplomatic contacts, the EU is facing uncomfortable questions about its own boycott of the junta.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Will elections in Israel change its Iran approach?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09767188b943a49baac4190f8ff36f1b31a4141bae75af10d0d2857792ae636c</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-elections-in-israel-change-its-iran-approach/a-79776122--d46c291154a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-elections-in-israel-change-its-iran-approach/a-79776122?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Israelis head to the polls, the country's conflict with Iran casts a long shadow over the ballot box. But any leadership changes in Israel may not be enough to shake up its grand strategy on Tehran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>A bad omen? Syria bans women from university courses</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3918fd2c0edb30fb440c5b9c7d06d3f98453a59600c256e6a475457a8f159ac6</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T20:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-bad-omen-syria-bans-women-from-university-courses/a-79769348--ba55f3eb7dc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-bad-omen-syria-bans-women-from-university-courses/a-79769348?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The recent announcement that Syrian tertiary institutes will not allow women into some courses has triggered debate. Critics worry it may be a sign that the new Syrian government is restricting women's rights.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why Ukraine may be involved in Mali's conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:988efd43528c2be9adf42912984d3ba19438ffb1d743016b3b776e40697c046e</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-ukraine-may-be-involved-in-mali-s-conflict/a-79743423--7ee87f683a22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-ukraine-may-be-involved-in-mali-s-conflict/a-79743423?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Allegations that Ukrainian specialists are supporting Tuareg rebels in Mali highlight Kyiv's effort to challenge Russian influence far beyond the battlefield in Europe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Merz in Asia as security issues loom large</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a42975ce424c1886ce8dd8828bdf850a88ac11c8559d0ab12570cea616117ad</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:32:00Z</published><