sing weight — and they're very popular with young people. They also claim to promote healthy growth in children. Is this true? How much protein is healthy?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda says it has no active Ebola cases, but infections in Kenya and Nigeria are prompting fresh scrutiny</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d685135631a9f4ae57f7e36dca57f41c122968703c6045deed534d18977e7b9</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T13:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uganda-says-it-has-no-active-ebola-cases-but-infections-in-kenya-and-nigeria-are-prompting-fresh-scr/a-79741580--819bf739b307.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uganda-says-it-has-no-active-ebola-cases-but-infections-in-kenya-and-nigeria-are-prompting-fresh-scrutiny/a-79741580?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Health officials are investigating whether Ebola patients in Kenya and Nigeria crossed paths at Uganda's main airport as conflicting accounts cloud the source of one infection.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Gadi Eisenkot campaigns on Moroccan roots in challenge to Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b70b4fde068229e7ba35461f8e3d543a0c8c13fde3a1932dd703b5168fca2a7</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T09:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gadi-eisenkot-campaigns-on-moroccan-roots-in-challenge-to-netanyahu/a-79747193--b8bf9b894fd4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gadi-eisenkot-campaigns-on-moroccan-roots-in-challenge-to-netanyahu/a-79747193?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Israel prepares to vote, Gadi Eisenkot is leveraging his Moroccan heritage in Likud strongholds such as Sderot. From historical divides to October 7, identity and trauma are redefining the city's political loyalties.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Prague honors Roma resistance fighters against Hitler</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6723fdf97545c3750e42904cbf5fa62cbe20d7520f7b8a567c5dff84319cf02</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T09:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/prague-honors-roma-resistance-fighters-against-hitler/a-79725015--c9d68b8992df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/prague-honors-roma-resistance-fighters-against-hitler/a-79725015?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than 1,400 Roma fought against the German Nazi occupation in Czechoslovakia. A new exhibition in Prague showcases the stories of partisans and soldiers whose fates barely received any attention for decades.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
